      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your husband is absolutely right to suggest Tylenol (acetaminophen) as it's generally considered safe to take during pregnancy as long as it's used at the recommended dosage. Acetaminophen can also help alleviate your headache. However, it's always advisable to consult with your healthcare provider or a pharmacist before starting any new medication during pregnancy, as they can advise on the appropriate dosage and safety. In terms of managing swelling, staying well-hydrated by drinking plenty of water can help, but if the swelling is significant or causing discomfort, it would be wise to discuss this with your doctor to rule out any serious conditions. If you're feeling very uncomfortable, now might be a good time to have that conversation, even if you just wanted to avoid the ER. Your health is the top priority, and seeking a doctor's advice now can save you from potential complications down the line.",
